.TH HALCYON 1 "November 2026" "halcyon 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
halcyon \- open HF data modem console
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B halcyon
[\fB\-\-host\fR \fIADDR\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B halcyon
starts the Halcyon modem console: a small HTTP server that serves the browser
user interface and its JSON control API.  The page shows the waterfall, the
speed ladder, the received frames and the transcript, and from it you connect
a radio, pick a speed level and send traffic.
.PP
The server binds to the loopback interface by default.  It has no
authentication, so do not bind it to a public or shared interface.
.PP
Radio access is provided by one of four transports: the Hermes Lite 2
protocol, TCI, CAT through Hamlib's
.BR rigctld (1),
or the simulated channel used by the bench console.  Connecting a radio does
not transmit: the transmit path stays disarmed until you arm it in the panel.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-host " \fIADDR\fR"
Address to bind.  Defaults to 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BR \-\-port " \fIPORT\fR"
TCP port to listen on.  Defaults to 8730.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/halcyon
The modem, the link layer, the radio clients and the web interface.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/halcyon-modem
The C++17 modem core, for encoding and decoding frames from a script.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B halcyon --port 8730
Serve the console at http://127.0.0.1:8730/ .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR halcyon-modem (1),
.BR rigctld (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The Halcyon authors.
